{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524653-where-do-you-get-your-names-for-player-characters-and-nonplayer-characters","id":1524653,"title":"Where do you get your names for player characters and nonplayer characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-28T11:39:13-07:00","id":1524653,"title":"Where do you get your names for player characters and nonplayer characters?","content":"I have a handful of books that male and female names throughout the world and it's quite handy when I'm stuck on a good name. So how do you go about your methods of naming pc's and npc's?<br /> <br /> I have a fondness for Latin, Greek, and Irish/Gaelic names myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T15:22:01-07:00","id":1524660,"title":"","content":"In terms of their names as mortals, I try to use whatever most makes sense given their history and background. I often use those online sites that give most popular baby names that you can find out by year. For games set in the US, they help a lot. And you can see which names are always popular and which ones rise and fall as fads over the years. If a chronicle is set in another place or time period, I try to read a little history that can provide details on the type of names that were used in that time period. Historical fiction can also help a lot.<br /> <br /> Of course, vampires often use aliases especially older ones. If they are trying to mix in mortal society, like Anabelle Triabelle being known as Ellen Stanley Greer, I use an appropriate name. And I do like the idea that some vampires have a specific &quot;vampire name&quot; that is obviously not their mortal name or what they use when interacting with mortals. Lodin, Modius, Erictho, Uriah, Balthazar, etc. are all examples. That's distinct from the vampire simply having a popular nickname that some or all people call them by (like Son). I will get more poetic and obscure with those because I am going for something unique.<br /> <br /> In all cases I try to keep each character unique so as not to confuse the players. And I try to use a name that is somehow distinctive of some element of the character whether it's their time period when they were embraced, an association with a famous person or literary character, a stereotype associated with the name, or something else. I'm not always successful with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}